                                                "sense_id": "6ff30caf-4244-304e-a43b-a4b1021949b5",
                                                "text": "I heard that she left off powder, patches, and rouge, for a month when his third consort died, and he grew religious—whether out of grief or gratitude, I never heard; then she grew factious, for the sake of your own King, and thought to strew the way to the altar with straws instead of flowers. I applaud her spirit in fighting for a crown."
